The SQL language is rich in keywords. Most SQL implementations do not allow keywords to be used as identifiers (names of tables or columns) unless they are enclosed in double-quotes. But SQLite is more flexible. Many keywords can be used as identifiers without needing to be quoted, as long as those keywords are used in a context where it is clear that they are intended to be an identifier. For example, the following statement is valid in SQLite:
